                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.00B/650: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >MacMurray</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peiping</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1929-10-17T17:00:00+08:00">October 17, 1929—5
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 5:05 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>896. Following from American Consul at Harbin: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“October 16, 10 a.m. Verdict case 38 prisoners Soviet Consulate raid
                            given out in prison yesterday. Five sentenced to nine years, 21 to
                            seven, 7 to five and 4 (women) to two. Chinese interpreter freed. Local
                            foreign opinion is that trial was a farce.”</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">MacMurray</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
